# These fixtures are byte-exact test data — their line-ending bytes are
# the entire point of internal/lineio's tests (PROCESS.md §3.1: crlf.txt
# and lf.txt must differ *only* in terminator bytes, byte-for-byte).
# Without this, a contributor checking out on Windows with the common
# core.autocrlf=true default silently gets lf.txt's LF bytes rewritten
# to CRLF on checkout, breaking that exact comparison — discovered while
# verifying the PROCESS.md §4 step 8 performance pass, not a
# hypothetical. `-text` disables any of git's own line-ending
# normalization for every file in this directory, regardless of the
# checking-out user's global config.
* -text
